urse_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062907/example-9357.json" "file_sha256" "7ff0a241ca921d482756c490fb510cdf8c8e510bfb7576953331bacb157c631c"} {"question" "e-9361" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\displaystyle{\\lim_{n \\to \\infty} \\left(1+\\dfrac{1}{n}\\right)^{nx/3}}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062907/example-9361.json" "file_sha256" "d40f413348f33545c99b4162483e5f1532a6e80a9ed827ccf0ceb900c719a45b"} {"question" "e-9361" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall the following special limit: \n\n$$\ne = \\lim_{n \\to  \\infty} \\left(1+\\dfrac{1}{n}\\right)^{n}\n$$\n\nNow, we rewrite the given limit using the algebra of limits, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{(1+\\frac{1}{n})}^{nx/3} & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{[{(1+\\frac{1}{n})}^{n}]}^{x/3} \\\\  & ={[{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{(1+\\frac{1}{n})}^{n}]}^{x/3} \\\\  & ={e}^{x/3} \\\\  & =\\sqrt[3]{{e}^{x}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062907/example-9361.json" "file_sha256" "d40f413348f33545c99b4162483e5f1532a6e80a9ed827ccf0ceb900c719a45b"} {"question" "e-9358" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\displaystyle{\\lim_{n \\to \\infty} \\left(1+\\dfrac{x}{n}\\right)^{-n/2}}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062907/example-9358.json" "file_sha256" "34dd99a4237ec1325edcdc25e273c099f172c5f6180f6788914a0cd056aa810c"} {"question" "e-9358" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall the following special limit: \n\n$$\ne^x = \\lim_{n \\to  \\infty} \\left(1+\\dfrac{x}{n}\\right)^{n}\n$$\n\nNow, we rewrite the given limit using the algebra of limits, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{(1+\\frac{x}{n})}^{-n/2} & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{[{(1+\\frac{x}{n})}^{n}]}^{-1/2} \\\\  & ={[{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{(1+\\frac{x}{n})}^{n}]}^{-1/2} \\\\  & ={({e}^{x})}^{-1/2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{{e}^{x}}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062907/example-9358.json" "file_sha256" "34dd99a4237ec1325edcdc25e273c099f172c5f6180f6788914a0cd056aa810c"}] "usage" {"e-9361" [] "e-9358" [] "e-9357" []} "basis" 2043 "retractions" [[17592186151964 :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle{\\lim_{n \\to \\infty} \\left(1+\\dfrac{1}{n}\\right)^{3n}}$."] [17592186151964 :question/worked-solution "Recall the following special limit:\n\n$$\ne = \\lim_{n \\to \\infty} \\left(1+\\dfrac{1}{n}\\right)^{n}\n$$\n\nNow, we rewrite the given limit using the algebra of limits, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\lim_{n \\to \\infty}(1 + \\frac{1}{n})^{3n} &= \\lim_{n \\to \\infty}[(1 + \\frac{1}{n})^{n}]^{3} \\\\\n&= [\\lim_{n \\to \\infty}(1 + \\frac{1}{n})^{n}]^{3} \\\\\n&= e^{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186151966 :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle{\\lim_{n \\to \\infty} \\left(1+\\dfrac{1}{n}\\right)^{nx/3}}$."] [17592186151966 :question/worked-solution "Recall the following special limit:\n\n$$\ne = \\lim_{n \\to \\infty} \\left(1+\\dfrac{1}{n}\\right)^{n}\n$$\n\nNow, we rewrite the given limit using the algebra of limits, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\lim_{n \\to \\infty}(1 + \\frac{1}{n})^{nx/3} &= \\lim_{n \\to \\infty}[(1 + \\frac{1}{n})^{n}]^{x/3} \\\\\n&= [\\lim_{n \\to \\infty}(1 + \\frac{1}{n})^{n}]^{x/3} \\\\\n&= e^{x/3} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt[3]{e^{x}}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186151965 :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle{\\lim_{n \\to \\infty} \\left(1+\\dfrac{x}{n}\\right)^{-n/2}}$."] [17592186151965 :question/worked-solution "Recall the following special limit:\n\n$$\ne^x = \\lim_{n \\to \\infty} \\left(1+\\dfrac{x}{n}\\right)^{n}\n$$\n\nNow, we rewrite the given limit using the algebra of limits, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\lim_{n \\to \\infty}(1 + \\frac{x}{n})^{-n/2} &= \\lim_{n \\to \\infty}[(1 + \\frac{x}{n})^{n}]^{-1/2} \\\\\n&= [\\lim_{n \\to \\infty}(1 + \\frac{x}{n})^{n}]^{-1/2} \\\\\n&= (e^{x})^{-1/2} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{\\frac{1}{e^{x}}}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
